      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-28T16:56:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The reason of \"FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_MATCH_PROCESSED_SET\" is preventing the attacker unlock template multiple times in a single nonce context.\n\nYes. I think I understand it now. To unlock the template, we need to provide UserID (LabelSeed). To match I need nonce context too. And there is only one match per single nonce context and one match when template is unlocked. Is it correct?\n\nIs the `dec_state-\u003eis_locked` responsible for locking templates when there was no match, e.g. user cancelled AuthSession?",
      "parentUuid": "439df580_420ddd04",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "39b88ed14ae7139542ef3e69204a7df9e657a6e5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
